Soch AI Script runs on 3 structured engines:

1️⃣ Hook Intelligence Engine
2️⃣ Story Architecture Engine
3️⃣ Retention Optimization Engine

Everything flows through these three.

1️⃣ HOOK INTELLIGENCE ENGINE
Purpose
Generate psychologically strong hooks based on topic + audience + tone.
Available Hook Systems
Pattern Interrupt
Personal Stakes
Curiosity Gap
Social Proof + FOMO
Immediate Threat / Reward
Auto-Selection Logic

Hook type is selected based on topic classification:

Achievement / ambition topics → Pattern Interrupt + Personal Stakes

Warning topics → Immediate Threat

Mystery / lesson topics → Curiosity Gap

Success comparison → Social Proof

Emotional storytelling → Personal Stakes

Default weight priority: Pattern Interrupt + Personal Stakes + Curiosity Gap

Hook Rules
Hook must:
Be 1–2 lines
Match emotional intensity level
Match selected tone
Match audience profile
Avoid generic motivational phrasing

2️⃣ STORY ARCHITECTURE ENGINE
Instead of one fixed structure, Soch AI uses adaptive story frameworks.
Every script follows:
HOOK
BODY
Optional CTA

But BODY structure depends on content type.

Available Story Models

A) Transformation Arc
Phase 1 – Struggle
Phase 2 – Pressure
Phase 3 – Internal Shift
Phase 4 – Determination
Best for: Self-growth, ambition, comeback stories.

B) Breakdown Arc
Point
Explanation
Example
Shift in perspective
Conclusion
Best for: Educational or insight-based content.

C) Warning Arc
Problem
Escalation
Consequence
Preventive Shift
Best for: Risk, mindset, caution-based topics.

D) Story + Lesson Hybrid
Story
Turning point
Lesson
Actionable takeaway
Best for: Entrepreneurs and creators.

3️⃣ RETENTION OPTIMIZATION ENGINE
This is where Soch differentiates.

Re-Hook Logic
Insert micro-hooks every 20–30 seconds for long-form.
Open Loops
Create unresolved tension inside script.
Emotional Escalation
Intensity gradually increases unless user selects a calm tone.
Pacing Adjustment

Duration mapping: 
30 sec → 90–120 words
1 min → 150–200 words
Custom → 150 words per minute
Short scripts → tight, aggressive
Long scripts → layered narrative

USER INPUT PANEL
User selects:
Duration
Language
Audience
Emotional Intensity (1–5)
Tone
CTA toggle

